// CRYPT SHIFT — COVEN — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CRYPT SHIFT as witch house and halloween trap — a game alternate of crypt, selectable
// from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Pitched down a whole step to G minor and played half-time at 140. The verse gives the
// whole A phrase at HALF speed to an old upright piano in octaves (a warped music box in
// the intro and outro), re-harmonised a chord a bar — Gm F Eb D Eb Cm6 D D7, the Cm6
// under "A, G" being the halloween chord — over a sliding 808 and a trap kit on three.
// The hook then arrives at its OWN speed on a pitched TR-808 cowbell, chopped into the
// phonk rhythm: each note starts on its original step and is re-struck on the
// sixteenths between. The climbing passage (bars 29–32 of the original) and the
// descending one (37–40) and the B phrase all come round. In the second hook a ghost
// voice sings the hook at half speed an octave down under the cowbell's full speed.
// Three voices are this song's own (voiceParams): the 808, which slides only where two
// notes are written to overlap, the pitched cowbell, and an old voice (the Announcer
// preset on the elder throat) saying "the coven rises" into both hooks.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the hook at half speed on a warped music box, choir (cabinet loop)
//   5–12   verse — the 808 drops; the A phrase at half speed on the upright
//   13–16  pre — the B phrase at its own speed, the cowbell teased, riser
//   17–24  GHOST CHOIR — no kit until 21, the choir sings, the music box replies
//   25–40  THE HOOK — phonk cowbell: A phrase twice, the climb, A phrase
//   41–44  bridge — the descending passage, kit on one and three only
//   45–48  build — the cowbell alone, snare roll, riser
//   49–64  THE HOOK two — the ghost voice at half speed; the climb; the B phrase
//   65–72  GHOST CHOIR two — the half-time kit stays, the upright replies
//   73–80  outro — music box, thinning kit; the loop returns to bar 5
// 
// WEATHER SYNC: the crypt eclipse runs on the heard song beat (CRYPT_WEATHER_TIMING,
// a 192-beat / 48-bar cycle counted from bar 1, whatever the tempo). Bars 17–24 and
// 65–72 — beats 64–96 of the first and second cycle — are the choir. The first time the
// kit drops out as the clouds gather on the last beats of bar 16; the second time a
// half-time kit stays under it. The hook (25) and the outro (73) come in as they clear,
// and the loop (5–80) ends on cycle beat 128, clear sky.
// 
// 80 bars at 140. Written by work/local/_crypt-remix-coven.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): the Ghost Choir swells in over its first two bars (17, 65).
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
